course: dictionary
lesson: 5446
title: Lander
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lander is a spacecraft built to land safely on the surface of a planet, a moon, a comet or an asteroid. Its job is to touch down and stay there.
explain: Context helps you work out the word. In «Mars lander» the place word tells you where it goes. In «lunar lander», lunar means "of the Moon", so it is a lander for the Moon. The phrase «the lander touched down» shows it came down to the ground.
explain: Compare it with other spacecraft. An orbiter circles high above, and a rover drives around on the ground after it has landed. A lander comes down and stays in one place. Real landers include the Apollo Lunar Module, Viking on Mars and Philae on a comet.
fact: A lander is a spacecraft built to land on a planet, moon, comet or asteroid.
fact: «Lunar» means "of the Moon", so a «lunar lander» is built to land on the Moon.
fact: An orbiter circles in space, a rover drives around, and a lander touches down and stays put.
fact: In 2014 Europe's Rosetta spacecraft dropped the lander Philae onto Comet 67P, the first landing on a comet.
fact: Less often, lander can mean a person who lands, or a person from a land, as in «Highlander».
exercise: «Europe's Rosetta spacecraft orbited Comet 67P and dropped the lander Philae onto it.» What is a lander? | A telescope that looks at stars | *A spacecraft built to land on a comet, moon or planet | A spacecraft that circles a planet and never comes down | A robot that drives around on Mars
exercise: In the phrase «lunar lander», what does lunar mean? | Made of ice | *Of the Moon | Very large | Of the sea
exercise: Which spacecraft circles a planet rather than landing on it? | A bacteriophage | *An orbiter | A lander | A rover
test: «Viking on Mars» is called a Mars lander. Why? | It was made of red paint | It orbits the Sun forever | *It landed on Mars | It was a planet
test: The Soviet Venera landers survived only about an hour or two. What destroyed them? | Being too slow to move | *The heat and pressure | Hungry animals | Running out of fuel on the way down
exam: The sentence «Bacteriophages look like tiny moon landers» helps us picture what? | A bacterium that flies to the Moon | A tiny moon with bacteria living on it | A doctor's tool for taking blood | *A tiny virus that lands on a bacterium, puts its instructions inside and bursts it
